      "id": "emergent_eu_compute_infrastructure_push",
      "description": "In response to persistent access vulnerabilities and the Sovereign Access Initiative's partial success, a coalition of EU member states launches a coordinated bid to nationalise or co-invest in critical domestic compute infrastructure, including Gigafactory Site B and regional AI clusters. The move aims to anchor frontier-scale training capacity under EU legal jurisdiction, directly addressing the sovereignty gap despite high fiscal and political costs.",
